<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 19407 0 R/Alt(Block diagram. A register FF1 on the left drives a combinational logic block, which drives the D input of a register FF2 on the right. Labels mark t_cq at the output of FF1, t_logic above the logic block, and t_su at the input of FF2. Below, the clock clk runs from the left through a shared buffer to the clock pin of FF1, labeled L1, and through the shared buffer and two more buffers to the clock pin of FF2, labeled L2. A note says t_skew = L2 - L1.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[116]/Pg 29232 0 R>>
